    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (last two digits of the registration year).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter, following the existing pattern for `customerCode`/`householdId`/`namesakeCount`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after the customer code and registration date are assigned, set the membership number via a new helper:\n   ```java\n   private static String generateMembershipNumber(String customerCode, LocalDate registrationDate) {\n       String yy = String.format(\"%02d\", registrationDate.getYear() % 100);\n       return customerCode + \"-M\" + yy;\n   }\n   ```\n   MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` maps the new field into `OwnerDto` automatically.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the JSON response.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added a `membership_number` column to the `owners` table, and appended the trailing value to the hsqldb `data.sql` seed inserts (which use positional `VALUES`, unlike the column-listed h2/postgres seeds).\n\nThe `registrationDate` defaults to the server's current date when omitted, so the derived membership number stays consistent with the two fields the test reads back (`SMI-0007-M26`-style).",
